   "notes": "Downing Place URC, north flank along Downing Street (p0 = east end). Buff ashlar Gothic flank with buttresses (pilasters), a pointed-arched doorway with red marble shafts near the east end, and paired tall lancets with red shafts per bay above a moulded band; red painted lettering on the plinth band. Only the eastern bay is clear in the oblique Mapillary view; the other bays repeat it by assumption."
